<GuideLayout 
  title="Custom Activewear MOQ Guide" 
  type="MOQ GUIDE"
  description="Compare stock trial quantities with OEM/ODM minimums per style and color. Confirm pcs versus sets, stock, sample costs and production timing before ordering."
>
  <h2>Understanding Minimum Order Quantities</h2>
  <p>MOQ must specify both the unit and the scope: pieces or complete sets, per style and, for OEM/ODM, per color. A stock trial and a new custom production run have different requirements.</p>
  
  <h3>MOQ Tiers at Fitclo</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Ready-stock trial: {businessFacts.readyStock.trial}</li>
    <li>Private label on existing stock: confirm the selected SKU, stock and branding method before setting a minimum.</li>
    <li>New OEM/ODM production: {businessFacts.oem.moq}</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Why Low MOQ Matters</h3>
  <p>Low MOQs allow you to test market demand, manage inventory risk, and launch a wider variety of designs with less upfront capital.</p>
  <p>{businessFacts.oem.sampleFee} {businessFacts.oem.sampleDevelopment} {businessFacts.oem.bulkProduction}</p>
</GuideLayout>
